{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>ושפח.</b> Like מספחת (Leviticus 13:6). And if it is with shin, then likewise בשורי מהם (Hosea 9:12):" "<b>פתהן.</b> Some say it is deficient alef: פאתהן, and the meaning is 'the crown of their heads.' But what is correct in my eyes is that it is from the root והפות (1 Kings 7:50), a hint to their hind parts; and so he mentioned above and below:" "<b>יערה.</b> He will uncover:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The comment addresses whether the word is spelled with sin or shin; the verse text reads וְשָׂפָח (with sin), but the lemma heading ושפח lacks the niqqud, leaving the consonantal identity ambiguous.", 1 "Resolved אומ' as אומרים based on context. The word 'deficient' (חסר) refers to missing-letter spelling."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:16.766414771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}